Settings: a cycles AGC; m opens Mic Gain; p edits Power; s edits Step Size; t cycles Tuner; v selects VFO; q returns with Back. Repeat a for the next AGC choice; each change is read back. AGC controls receiver recovery after signal strength changes, not microphone gain or transmitter ALC. Fast recovers sooner; Slow holds gain reduction longer. Choose by listening and consult the radio user guide. Yaesu cycles Fast, Mid, Slow, Auto, Off; Auto selects recovery for the mode and YAC announces the returned Auto speed. FTX-1 uses the selected Main/Sub receiver. Icom cycles Fast, Mid, Slow presets; FM and digital voice/data modes with fixed AGC report Fast fixed without writes. Icom preset timing, including a preset configured Off, is left unchanged. Kenwood TS-590SG/verified TS-480 cycle Fast, Slow, Off; FM is unavailable. Custom time constants are not edited. Off disables automatic gain regulation and received audio can vary more widely; adjust listening volume as needed. Unknown readings prevent changes; rejected or unconfirmed changes report failure. No transmission is required. QMX AGC is not implemented. h reads Settings help; h inside Mic Gain reads its full procedure.

